ILLUSION_HASH_PREDICT_HEAD|schema=ILLUSION_HASH_PREDICTION_V1|date=2026-11-09|author=the local Opus 5.5 seat, pid 8467a937cba309f7 (prediction agent)|named_sources=Welch_1974;Lubkin_1978;Page_1993;Ji_Liu_Song_2018;Brakerski_Shmueli_2019;Dehaene_De_Moor_2003;Van_den_Nest_2010;MacWilliams_1969;Landsberg_1893;MacWilliams_Sloane_1977_ch13|formula_tag=NAMED_for_HAAR_DERIVED_for_the_rest|measurement_status=NOT_RUN|written_before_any_measurement=1|states_built=0|density_matrices_built=0|function_tables_built=0|sums_over_functions=0|index_tuple_checks=frame_n<=4_purity_n<=6_local_formal_n<=5|integer_only=1|rational_format=num:den_reduced_den_positive|ensembles=HAAR,GLOBAL_2,GLOBAL_3,GLOBAL_4,GLOBAL_5,LOCAL_2,LOCAL_3,LOCAL_4,LOCAL_5,QUAD_2|n_range=1..8|k_range=0..n|t_range=1..4|split=first_k_qubits_vs_rest|script=predict_hash.py|script_sha256=dc63691cc6bcb6bab70ec132fd947034e85608d992649718f7c9da9df7db6a81|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D01_HAAR_FRAME|tag=NAMED|text=F_t(HAAR)=1:binom(N+t-1,t), the inverse dimension of Sym^t(C^N); every ensemble has F_t>=F_t(HAAR) (Welch bound) with equality iff it is an exact t-design; design order = largest t with equality|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D02_HAAR_PURITY|tag=NAMED|text=E Tr rho_A^2=(d_A+d_B):(N+1) (Lubkin 1978, Page 1993); route 2: Tr[(SWAP_A x 1_B)(1+SWAP)]:(N(N+1))=(d_A d_B^2+d_A^2 d_B):(N(N+1))|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D03_GLOBAL_FRAME|tag=DERIVED|text=<psi_f,psi_g>=N^-1 sum_x w^(g(x)-f(x)); h=g-f is uniform over all functions so z_x=w^h(x) are iid uniform q-th roots of unity and F_t=N^(-2t) E abs(sum_x z_x)^(2t); E z^m=[m=0 mod q] so E abs(S)^(2t)=number of pairs of t-tuples X,Y in [N]^t with count_x(X)=count_x(Y) mod q at every x; grouped by the multiset (type) of nonzero per-point pairs (a,b) with a=b mod q: count=sum_types N!:((N-m)! prod mu!) * (t!)^2:prod(a! b!), m=parts, mu=multiplicities; a polynomial in N of degree t; route 2 a point-by-point DP, route 3 a residue-class count of t-tuples for N<=16|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D04_GLOBAL_Q_LADDER|tag=DERIVED|text=for q>t the condition a=b mod q with 0<=a,b<=t forces a=b, so GLOBAL_q equals uniform continuous U(1) phases (PHASE_U1) for every t<q; for t>=q the types with (q,0) and (0,q) add strictly positive terms when N>=2; leading coefficient: each part has a+b>=2, so t parts need weight 2 each: only (1,1) for q>=3 giving c_t=t!, and also (2,0),(0,2) for q=2 giving c_t=(2t-1)!!|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D05_LIMITS|tag=DERIVED|text=F_t(HAAR)=t!:(N(N+1)..(N+t-1))=t! N^-t (1-binom(t,2):N+O(N^-2)); with count=c_t N^t+c_(t-1) N^(t-1)+..: F:F_HAAR -> c_t:t!; when c_t=t!: (F-F_HAAR) N^(t+1) -> L_t=c_(t-1)+t! binom(t,2) and (F:F_HAAR-1) N -> L_t:t!; so (F-F_HAAR) N^2 -> 0 for t>=2|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D06_GLOBAL_PURITY|tag=DERIVED|text=x=(a,b); Tr rho_A^2=N^-2 sum_(a,a2,b,b2) w^(f(a,b)-f(a2,b)+f(a2,b2)-f(a,b2)); over uniform f a term has expectation 1 iff the net coefficient at every point is 0 mod q, else 0; a=a2 or b=b2: corners cancel in pairs; a!=a2 and b!=b2: four distinct points, each net coefficient +1 or -1, and +-1 is nonzero mod q for every q>=2, so q=2 brings no extra cancellation (f(a,b)+f(a2,b)+f(a,b2)+f(a2,b2) mod 2 is a uniform bit, E(-1)^bit=0); survivors d_A d_B^2+d_A^2 d_B-d_A d_B; E Tr rho_A^2=(d_A+d_B-1):N for every q>=2; minus HAAR = -(d_A-1)(d_B-1):(N(N+1)); route 2 counts index quadruples for n<=6|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D07_LOCAL_FRAME|tag=DERIVED|text=psi_f = tensor_i (w^h_i(0) ket0 + w^h_i(1) ket1):sqrt2; overlaps factor over qubits with independent h_i so F_t(LOCAL_q,n)=F_t(GLOBAL_q,1)^n; route 2 per qubit: abs(overlap)^2=(2+z+conj z):4, z=w^delta, delta uniform in Z_q, factor=4^-t sum_(i+j+l=t) t!:(i!j!l!) 2^i [j=l mod q]|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D08_LOCAL_PURITY|tag=DERIVED|text=each psi_f is a product state over qubits so rho_A is pure: Tr rho_A^2=1 for every f and every split; PREDICTION min=mean=max=1; route 2: f(a,b)=H_A(a)+H_B(b) so the four-corner exponent vanishes identically: the formal coefficient of every variable h_i(v) is 0 for all N^2 quadruples (counted for n<=5, every q, every split)|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D09_QUAD_FRAME|tag=DERIVED|text=h=f+g is again a uniform QUAD_2 form; S=sum_x (-1)^h(x); A=B+B^T is a uniform alternating GF(2) matrix; abs(S)^2=N sum_(u in rad A) (-1)^h(u); h is additive on rad A and uniform c makes h restricted to rad A a uniform linear functional, so abs(S:N)^2=2^(-2r) with probability 2^-(n-2r) and 0 otherwise, rank A=2r; F_t=2^-n sum_r P(rank A=2r) 2^(2r(1-t)) for t>=1; alternating counts T(n,2r) by bordering T(n+1,2r)=4^r T(n,2r)+(2^n-4^(r-1)) T(n,2r-2) and by the MacWilliams 1969 product|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D10_QUAD_VS_GLOBAL2|tag=DERIVED|text=route 2: E(-1)^(sum of h over 2t points)=1 iff the odd-multiplicity support lies in RM(2,n)^perp=RM(n-3,n), minimum weight 8, weight-8 words = affine 3-flats (MacWilliams-Sloane 1977 ch.13); so F_t(QUAD_2)=F_t(GLOBAL_2) for t<=3 and F_4(QUAD_2)-F_4(GLOBAL_2)=8! 2^(n-3) [n,3]_2 : N^8 for n>=3, 0 for n<3|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D11_QUAD_PURITY|tag=DERIVED|text=four-corner exponent=(a+a2)^T M (b+b2) with M=B_AB the k x (n-k) cross block (Q_A, Q_B and c cancel) so Tr rho_A^2=2^-rank_GF2(M) for every state; mean from rank counts prod_(i<r) (2^k-2^i)(2^(n-k)-2^i):(2^r-2^i) (Landsberg 1893) and a row recurrence; route 3: #(u: u^T M=0)=2^(k-r), its mean is 1+(2^k-1)2^-(n-k), so E 2^-r=2^-k+2^-(n-k)-2^-n=(d_A+d_B-1):N, the GLOBAL_q mean|json=0
DERIVATION|id=D12_SCOPE|tag=DERIVED|text=splits are the first k qubits against the rest; every ensemble here is invariant under qubit permutations, so any k-subset gives the same mean; GLOBAL_q purity does not depend on q; F_t does not depend on the split; F_0=1 by definition (abs(.)^0=1)|json=0
